ctural) runs.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py` \u2014 Typer CLI `create`/`finalize`/`validate` commands (lines 286, 458-540) route through the same `operations.py` functions \u2014 a fix in `operations.py` covers both CLI and MCP surfaces without touching this file.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 MCP `sam_plan` action dispatch (`_sam_plan_create` line 214, `_sam_plan_finalize` line 352-370) \u2014 thin wrappers over `operations.py`, same conclusion.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/{local_yaml.py:716, github_task.py:560, beads.py:972}` \u2014 each backend's `finalize_plan` only flips state; no structural check. A fix belongs above this layer (in `operations.py`), not duplicated three times per backend.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 the LLM-instruction-only enforcement (Bookend Task Generation + self-check step 12) is the *sole* current enforcement mechanism, and it is advisory (agent-followed), not machine-checked.\\n\\n## Code-Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/t0-baseline-capture.md` \u2014 reads `acceptance-criteria-structured` from the plan; assumes it is being invoked at all (i.e., assumes a T0 task exists to dispatch it).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/tn-verification-gate.md` \u2014 same assumption for TN; produces the `TN-verification` artifact that `complete-implementation` reads.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` (lines 300-324) \u2014 Pre-Phase-1 TN Verification Check treats an absent `TN-verification` artifact as \\\"no structured criteria, proceed\\\" (mermaid label line 318: `\\\"No structured criteria \u2014 proceed to Phase 1\\\"`). This label is factually wrong when criteria exist but bookends were never generated \u2014 it silently masks exactly the failure mode #3277 describes. This is the concrete downstream harm.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 \\\"Bookend Task Ordering\\\" section documents dispatch-ordering guarantees (T0 first, TN last) that don't hold if bookends were never created; nothing in the dispatch loop notices their absence (confirmed no bookend logic in `sam_schema/dispatch.py` or `core/quality_gates.py`).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` (line 33) \u2014 descriptive reference to `tn-verification-gate` re-running `acceptance-criteria-structured` checks; not a second gate, just documentation of intent.\\n\\n## Code-Other-References\\n\\n- `sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 `Task.is_bookend` / `Task.bookend_type` fields (lines 220-224), `BookendType` enum (line 105), `Plan.acceptance_criteria_structured` (line 298). Schema source of truth; unaffected by a fix but must stay in sync with any validator wiring change.\\n- `sam_schema/core/task_backend_types.py`, `sam_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py`, `sam_schema/readers/{manifest_reader,normalize,frontmatter_reader,yaml_reader}.py`, `sam_schema/core/backends/{memory,content,gist_task_layer}.py`, `sam_schema/cli_inputs.py` \u2014 all touch `bookend`/`is-bookend`/`acceptance-criteria-structured` field plumbing (serialize/deserialize/normalize) but contain no structural enforcement logic; grep-confirmed, no behavior change expected from a fix scoped to enforcement wiring.\\n- `sam_schema/dispatch.py`, `sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 grep-confirmed to contain **no** bookend-specific logic, consistent with `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`'s claim that \\\"No special handling is needed in the dispatch loop\\\" (T0/TN dispatch via ordinary priority/dependency ordering).\\n\\n## Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 P4_BOOKEND flow (lines 395-421) and TN-artifact consumption (lines 533-547, 565-567) document the intended contract accurately but describe it as a given, with no mention that enforcement is currently instruction-only.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 `is-bookend`/`bookend-type` field docs (lines 292-293, 388-389); accurate, no change needed for a validator-wiring fix.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/README.md`, `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` \u2014 user-facing T0/TN descriptions; accurate at a high level, no change needed.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/*.json`, `docs/workflow-result.json`, `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `graphify-out/*` \u2014 generated snapshots (confirmed via \\\"Last generated\\\" / `snapshot_status: historical-generated-output` markers). **Do not hand-edit.** If the fix restructures `swarm-task-planner.md`'s Bookend Task Generation section or self-check, run `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh` afterward per that skill's own trigger condition.\\n\\n## Configuration/CI\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` (line 244, `uv run -q --locked pytest`) \u2014 already runs `tests_sam/test_dependencies.py`'s full `BookendValidator` unit suite; these pass today and will continue to pass regardless of whether the validator is ever wired in, so CI green is not evidence the underlying defect is fixed. No existing CI job asserts end-to-end that a `finalize`/`create` call is rejected when structured criteria exist without bookends \u2014 that is a coverage gap this item's fix should close (new test in `tests_sam/` exercising `operations.create_plan`/`finalize_plan`, not just the validator class directly).\\n- No other workflow (`auto-rebase.yml`, `backlog-sync.yml`, `bump-marketplace.yml`, `claude-code-review.yml`, `claude.yml`, `copilot-setup-steps.yml`, `main-ci-health-check.yml`, `quality-gate-audit.yml`) references `sam_schema`, `tests_sam`, or `swarm-task-planner` \u2014 grep-confirmed, none affected.\\n\\n## Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 Bookend Task Generation (\u00a7328-391) and self-check step 12 (\u00a7605-612) are the only current enforcement mechanism and are advisory/LLM-followed, not machine-checked. This is the root-cause candidate for \\\"instruction-following failure\\\" \u2014 but the presence of an unwired, fully-correct `BookendValidator` (finding #5-9 above) means the more durable fix is schema-level enforcement, not a stronger prompt. Both should be considered candidate fixes; classification agent should weigh instruction-strengthening vs. schema-gap-closing as the primary vs. defense-in-depth remedy.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/t0-baseline-capture.md`, `agents/tn-verification-gate.md` \u2014 consumers, no changes needed for a validator-wiring fix; cross-listed above.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` \u2014 descriptive-only reference, no changes needed.\\n\\n## Ecosystem Completeness Checklist (5-question pass on the material systems)\\n\\n**`BookendValidator` (dependencies.py) + its absent call sites (operations.py/server.py/backends):**\\n1. What breaks if this changes (validator gets wired in)? \u2014 Plans with structured criteria and no T0/TN will start failing `create`/`finalize`/`append_task` where they previously silently succeeded. This is the intended fix but is a **breaking change for any in-flight drafting-state plan** that already lacks bookends (including `Pb31107bf` itself, if still in drafting/ready state) \u2014 needs a migration/backfill note, not just a code change.\\n2. Who/what consumes this? \u2014 CLI (`sam_plan.py`), MCP (`server.py`), all three backends transitively; ultimately `implement-feature`/`complete-implementation` skills and the T0/TN agents.\\n3. Is there a test guarding it? \u2014 Yes at the unit level (`test_dependencies.py`), **no** at the integration level (`operations.py` call path) \u2014 this is the gap to close.\\n4. Does documentation reference it accurately? \u2014 `backlog-item-lifecycle.md` and `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` describe the intended contract but not that enforcement is currently absent; no doc change strictly required by a wiring fix, but the lifecycle doc could note the new hard-fail behavior post-fix.\\n5. Backward-compat/migration concern? \u2014 Yes (see #1): existing plans/backlog items with structured criteria and missing bookends will need either a migration script (see `plugins/development-harness/scripts/migrate_plan_artifacts.py` as a precedent pattern) or a one-time audit before the validator is made hard-enforcing.\\n\\n**`complete-implementation` TN Verification Check mermaid (SKILL.md:317-318):**\\n1. What breaks if this changes? \u2014 Correcting the \\\"artifact absent \u21d2 no structured criteria\\\" label to distinguish \\\"no structured criteria\\\" from \\\"criteria exist but bookends missing\\\" changes orchestrator behavior from silent-proceed to a warn-or-block path for the latter case.\\n2. Who/what consumes this? \u2014 The orchestrator running `/dh:complete-implementation`.\\n3. Is there a test guarding it? \u2014 No automated test found for this SKILL.md's mermaid/procedure text (it's prose/diagram, not code) \u2014 verification is manual/agent-followed only.\\n4. Does documentation reference it accurately? \u2014 This IS the documentation; it is the artifact that needs correcting.\\n5. Backward-compat concern? \u2014 Low \u2014 tightening this check only adds a new warn/block branch; does not remove existing behavior for the already-passing case.\\n\\nSTATUS: DONE \u2014 Impact Radius written (16-row systems inventory, 6 categories, scope expansion flagged: BookendValidator exists but is never called from any plan create/finalize path \u2014 schema-level gap, not just an agent instruction-following miss).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:33:51.404839Z</sub>\\n\\nNone blocking. No other in-flight backlog item or plan must land first. The fix is self-contained to the write-path layer and its test suite; it does not require schema migrations or changes to plan file formats already in use.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:33:51.404599Z</sub>\\n\\nP2 (unchanged). Justification: the defect silently disables an independent verification safety net rather than causing an immediate, visible failure \u2014 `complete-implementation`'s Pre-Phase-1 check degrades gracefully (and misleadingly) to \\\"no structured criteria, proceed,\\\" so no plan is blocked or crashes. But because every plan with structured acceptance criteria is affected, the erosion of guarantees is systemic and ongoing, not a one-off edge case \u2014 this is a real correctness gap in a documented quality gate, not a cosmetic issue.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:33:51.404687Z</sub>\\n\\n- Restores the documented \\\"bookend tasks run automatically\\\" guarantee (`implement-feature/SKILL.md`'s Bookend Task Ordering section) so it reflects actual runtime behavior instead of an aspirational contract.\\n- Closes the false-confidence gap in `complete-implementation`'s Pre-Phase-1 check: a plan with structured acceptance criteria will either get real T0/TN verification or the gate will correctly flag that verification is missing, instead of both cases looking identical.\\n- Makes `BookendValidator`'s existing, fully-tested logic actually load-bearing \u2014 the unit test suite starts validating something that runs in production, not just a fixture-only correctness check.\\n- Applies uniformly across CLI, MCP, and all three backends by fixing one shared layer (`operations.py`), so no follow-up work is needed per backend.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:24:06.437017Z</sub>\\n\\nMISSION_ALIGNED \u2014 Wiring the existing BookendValidator into the plan write path reconnects an already-built, already-tested validator back to its intended enforcement point and fulfills the documented core workflow promise.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n**Stated Mission**: development-harness README \u00a7Implement-feature \u00a796 explicitly documents: \\\"Bookend tasks run automatically: T0 captures baseline state before implementation begins, TN verifies acceptance criteria after all implementation tasks finish.\\\" This is a core workflow guarantee, not an optional feature.\\n\\n**Architect Commit**: commit `5b150f7ac feat(sam-schema): add T0/TN bookend validation for SAM plans` (March 15, 2026) added:\\n  - `BookendValidator` class (dependencies.py, lines 276-391) with 5 structural rules including the exact rule this defect violates\\n  - 462 lines of unit test coverage in `test_dependencies.py`  \\n  - Full schema integration: `Plan.acceptance_criteria_structured` field, `Task.is_bookend` / `Task.bookend_type` fields\\n  - Agent instructions in swarm-task-planner (\u00a7328-391, Bookend Task Generation)\\n  - Consumer agents (`t0-baseline-capture`, `tn-verification-gate`) ready to execute T0/TN tasks\\n  - Skill documentation (`implement-feature`, `complete-implementation`) describing the dispatch ordering\\n\\n**Gap**: The validator exists and is correct in isolation, but is never invoked from `operations.py::create_plan`, `append_task`, or `finalize_plan` \u2014 the only call sites that could enforce the rule. This is a schema-level implementation gap (dead code), not a design divergence.\\n\\n**Alignment Verdict**: A fix that wires `BookendValidator` into the plan write path (likely `operations.py::finalize_plan` to guard state transitions, per the Impact Radius) restores the intended enforcement layer for a promise already documented, already designed, already tested at the unit level, and already installed in the SAM schema and agent instruction set. This is reconnecting a built solution to its call site, not introducing new functionality or diverging from stated product intent.\\n\\n**Secondary Effect** (positive): The fix closes the `complete-implementation` SKILL.md logic gap (Pre-Phase 1 TN Verification Check, line 318) where \\\"artifact absent\\\" is conflated with \\\"no structured criteria\\\" \u2014 once T0/TN generation is guaranteed by schema-level enforcement, the orchestrator can reliably distinguish these cases and provide clearer diagnostics.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:33:51.404745Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Given a plan-write call (`create_plan`, `finalize_plan`, or `append_task`, via CLI or MCP, on any of the three backends) where the resulting plan has a non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` list and is missing a `t0-baseline` task, a `tn-verification` task, or correct bookend dependency wiring, the call fails/is rejected rather than succeeding silently.\\n2. Given the same call with a non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` list and both bookend tasks correctly present, the call succeeds unchanged from current behavior.\\n3. Given a plan-write call where `acceptance-criteria-structured` is empty, bookend presence is not required and the call is unaffected by this fix.\\n4. Re-running plan `Pb31107bf`'s creation/finalization path (or an equivalent reproduction with a non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` list) demonstrates the previously-silent gap is now caught.\\n5. An automated test exists that exercises the enforcement through `operations.py` (not just `BookendValidator` in isolation) and fails prior to the fix, passes after.\\n6. `tests_sam/test_dependencies.py`'s existing `BookendValidator` unit tests continue to pass unmodified.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:33:51.404713Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen `create_plan`, `finalize_plan`, or `append_task` is called (via CLI or MCP, on any backend) with a plan whose `acceptance-criteria-structured` list is non-empty, the operation validates bookend presence (via `BookendValidator` or equivalent logic) before the write succeeds. A plan lacking exactly one `t0-baseline` task and one `tn-verification` task under those conditions is rejected (or corrected, per the remediation approach chosen during planning) rather than silently persisted. Plans with an empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` list are unaffected and continue to skip bookend requirements.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:33:51.404865Z</sub>\\n\\nSmall/bounded integration task, not a redesign. Scope is well-defined: instantiate and call an already-complete, already-tested validator from 3 known functions in one file (`operations.py`), plus add one integration test. No new validation logic needs to be written \u2014 `BookendValidator`'s rules are correct as-is per Root-Cause Analysis. Estimate: S (single focused implementation task, suitable for one task in the next SAM plan).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:33:51.404529Z</sub>\\n\\n**Reproducible: systemic, not plan-specific.** Any plan write (`create_plan`, `finalize_plan`, `append_task`) that carries a non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` list will exhibit this defect, because all three operations route through the same unguarded write-path layer in `dh_core/operations.py` \u2014 independent of backend (local YAML, GitHub, beads) or entry surface (CLI, MCP).\\n\\nSteps to reproduce:\\n1. Run `dh:swarm-task-planner` (or call `sam_plan` with `action: create`/`finalize`) on any feature spec that yields at least one `acceptance-criteria-structured` entry.\\n2. Read the resulting plan (`sam_plan(action=\\\"read\\\")`).\\n3. Observe the task list contains no task with `bookend-type: t0-baseline` and no task with `bookend-type: tn-verification`, despite the non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` array.\\n\\nConfirmed instance: plan `Pb31107bf` \u2014 6 `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries (AC1\u2013AC6), task list exactly `[T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, T6]`, no T0/TN, verified via direct `sam_plan` MCP read.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 development-harness /dh:work-backlog-item work --auto #3268, plan Pb31107bf\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:15:33.805649Z</sub>\\n\\n## 5-Whys Chain\\n\\n**CLAIM 1: Plan Pb31107bf with non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` has zero bookend tasks**\\n- EVIDENCE: Direct plan read via SAM MCP tool \u2014 plan shows 6 `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries and task list [T1\u2013T6] with no T0 or TN tasks\\n- VERIFIED: yes\\n\\n**CLAIM 2: swarm-task-planner has a documented mandatory self-check at Phase 4 Step 12 that should validate bookend presence**\\n- EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` lines 605-612: \\\"Bookend presence check (when `acceptance-criteria-structured` is non-empty)\\\" mandates exactly one T0, one TN, proper dependencies; failure blocks registration\\n- VERIFIED: yes\\n\\n**CLAIM 3: A `BookendValidator` class exists in sam_schema with full unit test coverage and encodes all bookend validation rules**\\n- EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` lines 276-391 define `BookendValidator` class with methods to query T0, TN, implementation tasks, and validate dependency chains\\n- VERIFIED: yes\\n\\n**CLAIM 4: BookendValidator is exported from sam_schema package but never called from any plan write path**\\n- EVIDENCE: Bash \u2014 `grep -r \\\"BookendValidator\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" plugins/development-harness/ | grep -v test_` returns only: `__init__.py` (export), `core/dependencies.py` (definition). Zero calls from `create_plan`, `finalize_plan`, or `append_task` in `dh_core/operations.py` or backends.\\n- VERIFIED: yes\\n- DEPENDS ON: Claim 3\\n\\n**CLAIM 5: The agent's Phase 4 Step 12 self-check is either never executed or the check logic itself is incomplete, because no validation gate exists in the control flow**\\n- EVIDENCE: The control flow from plan creation \u2192 plan finalization follows `dh_core/operations.py:create_plan()` \u2192 backend write \u2192 no `BookendValidator` instantiation or call anywhere in the path. The agent's documented self-check instruction (CLAIM 2) cannot execute a schema validation that exists outside the agent's scope.\\n- VERIFIED: yes\\n- DEPENDS ON: Claims 1, 2, 4\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\n**Code/Schema Gap**: A `BookendValidator` exists with complete logic and full unit test coverage, but is structurally isolated from the plan-write operations (`create_plan`, `finalize_plan`, `append_task`). The validator is never instantiated or called from any backend or MCP handler. Therefore, even a correctly-behaving swarm-task-planner agent cannot trigger the validation \u2014 it has no effect on runtime behavior.\\n\\nThe immediate cause of plan Pb31107bf's missing bookends is that no schema validation layer enforced the bookend-presence rule at plan-registration time. The root cause is the design gap between where validation logic lives (isolated validator class) and where it needs to execute (in the write paths).\\n\\n**Why the gap exists**: The validator was implemented (sam_schema/core/dependencies.py) and tested, but the integration \u2014 calling it from `create_plan`, `finalize_plan`, or `append_task` \u2014 was never completed. This is traceable to a missing wire-up task between the validator's completion and the write-path integration, not to agent behavior or documentation issues.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"01ad8fa420e1ce2e31ecf1a2ce25b504d7d8043059148b548817f80124ee6cef\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRR3Nrg\"}"}